 61FE c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2013Ra17:                          
 61FE2c  Phys Rev C 88, 014307 (2013).                                          
 61FE c  Compiled by E. McNeice and B. Singh (McMaster), Sept 5, 2013.          
 61FE c  {+61}Mn produced in induced fission of uranium at ISOLDE, CERN         
 61FE2c  facility. E(proton)=1.4 GeV beam impinged a UC{-x} target of thickness 
 61FE3c  45 g/cm{+2}. Reaction products where ionized by RILIS and              
 61FE4c  separated based on their A/Q ratio using a High-Resolution Separator.  
 61FE5c  {+61}Mn obtained in the reaction was implanted on an aluminized mylar  
 61FE6c  tape for the decay. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, half-life using      
 61FE7c  three plastic |DE |b detectors and two MiniBall |g-detector clusters.  
 61FE8c  Deduced levels, J, |p, |b feeding intensities, log {Ift}. Comparison   
 61FE9c  with {+59}Fe data, and with shell-model calculations.                  
 61FE cB LOGFT$ Deduced by the compilers using log| {Ift} computer code         
 61FE cG RI(A)$ From |g|g-coin data; transition not seen in singles spectrum    
 61FE cL E$ From least-squares fit (by compilers) to E|g values. Reduced        
 61FE2cL |h{+2}=2.1 is somewhat larger than critical |h{+2}=1.7                 
 61MN  P 0.0         (5/2)-            0.708 S   8              7178      3     
 61MN cP T$ From time decay curves for several strongest |g rays (2013Ra17)     
 61MN cP J$ From Adopted Levels of {+61}Mn in ENSDF database                    
 61MN cP QP$ From 2012Wa38.                                                     
 61FE  N  0.363    7            1.0                                             
 61FE cN NR$ Deduced by 2013Ra17, based on I|b=33% {1} to g.s. of {+61}Fe       
 61FE2cN deduced from known normalization of decay scheme of {+61}Fe to {+61}Co 
 61FE cN BR$%B-N|<0.2 to first excited state in {+60}Fe (2013Ra17) from upper   
 61FE2cN limit of intensity of 824|g (from first 2+ to g.s. in {+60}Fe). Total  
 61FE3cN %|b{+-}n could not be determined due to long half-life of {+60}Fe.     
 61FE4cN 2013Ra17 use %|b{+-}n=0.6 {I1} from 2000HaZL (Thesis by Hannawald,     
 61FExcN Mainz 2000)                                                            
